desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Claude Settings Auto Enable MCP Generic",
	title_zh: "检测到Claude Settings Auto Enable MCP Generic",
	type: vuln,
	level: middle,
	rule_id: "source-config-claude-settings-auto-enable-mcp-generic",
	risk: "Security",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `claude-settings-auto-enable-mcp-generic` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/ai/ai-best-practices/claude-settings-auto-enable-mcp/claude-settings-auto-enable-mcp.yaml).
Original message: "enableAllProjectMcpServers" is set to true in settings. This automatically enables all MCP servers defined in project configuration without user confirmation, allowing malicious repositories to register arbitrary MCP servers that execute code on your machine. Remove this setting or set it to false so that MCP servers require explicit approval.

CWE: CWE-862: Missing Authorization
References:
- https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/security
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://pos/settings.json": <<<POS
"enableAllProjectMcpServers"
 

     	 :
 		

	true

POS,
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG,
)

${/.*\/settings\.json/}.pattern_regex(/"enableAllProjectMcpServers"\s*:\s*true/) as $p0
${/.*\/\.claude\/.*/}.pattern_regex(/"enableAllProjectMcpServers"\s*:\s*true/) as $p1
${/.*\/[^\/]*\.settings\.json/}.pattern_regex(/"enableAllProjectMcpServers"\s*:\s*true/) as $p2
$p0 + $p1 + $p2 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Claude Settings Auto Enable MCP Generic",
	title_zh: "检测到Claude Settings Auto Enable MCP Generic",
	message: "Claude Settings Auto Enable MCP Generic",
}
